@startuml clinical-workflow
' Workflow with the system (target) — DIP-27
' Source of diagrams/export/clinical-workflow.png
' Described in docs/07-architecture/target-system.md, sections 4 and 5.
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #444444
}
skinparam swimlane {
  TitleFontStyle bold
}

title Workflow with the system (target)

|Monitor and MIS|
start
:Vital signs charted every hour;\nlaboratory results released;
|System|
:Hourly cycle: read new values\n(MIS adapter; replay of PhysioNet in the diploma);
:Validate values; build features\nfrom past hours only;
if (Key vital sign recorded\nin the last 4 h?) then (no)
  :State "insufficient data":\nno risk, no alert;\nthe nurse is asked to measure;
  note left
    The new measurement
    is used at the next
    hourly cycle.
  end note
else (yes)
  |System|
  :Compute risk and the five\nmost influential measurements;
  if (Risk at or above threshold and not suppressed,\nor risk rose further since the last alert?) then (yes)
    :Alert: patient moves to the top,\n"72% · High risk" in red, banner;
    note right
      Not acknowledged in 30 min:
      marked "not acknowledged"
      at the top of the list.
    end note
    |ICU nurse|
    :Opens the patient view:\nreasons, trends, time since each measurement;
    :Re-checks the patient at the bedside\nand repeats the measurements;
    if (Change confirmed?) then (yes)
      :Informs the responsible physician;
      :Acknowledges: "physician informed";
      |Physician|
      :Assesses with the national sepsis protocol:\nqSOFA / SOFA, lactate, blood cultures;
      :Decides on treatment\n(outside the system);
    else (no)
      |ICU nurse|
      :Acknowledges: "change not confirmed"\n(kept as evidence of false alerts);
    endif
  else (no)
    |System|
    :Update list and trends;\nno alert;
  endif
endif
|System|
:Store prediction, alert, acknowledgement\nand audit record;
stop
@enduml
